at the Standard Life charge comparison is based on the wrong fund value. This, combined with the contradictory cost comparison figures (page 8 says 0.08% saving; page 11 table shows +0.26% increase), represents a material internal inconsistency on a figure relevant to the recommendation rationale for Standard Life. The chart label swap (A/D labels reversed between two charts on page 13) is a presentation inconsistency but does not affect underlying values. The 2.94%/2.95% mid growth rate discrepancy is a low-severity rounding issue. Overall, the most material findings are: the two inconsistent total pension values stated in the narrative (£110,000 and £106,000 versus the actual sum of £116,998.47); and the contradictory Standard Life charge impact figures (page 8 versus page 11 table), the latter of which rests on a charge row computed against the wrong plan value.","citations":[{"passageId":"P22","source":"Aviva Policy Info.md","category":"E","quote":"Plan value\n\n£3,744.36\n\nTransfer value\n\n£3,744.36\n\nWe've based these figures on the values as at 22 September 2025 .","cells":null},{"passageId":"P22","source":"Aviva Policy Info.md","category":"E","quote":null,"cells":["Aviva Pensions My Future Focus Consolidation (Pre-2024) S2","£1.8140","2,064.1433","£3,744.36","B9JLKB7"]},{"passageId":"P18","source":"Zurich Policy Info.md","category":"E","quote":null,"cells":["Managed AP (accumulation)","492.05","£210.221","£103,439.24"]},{"passageId":"P14","source":"Standard_Life_Policy_Info.md","category":"E","quote":null,"cells":["Value of investment","£3,002.02"]},{"passageId":"P14","source":"Standard_Life_Policy_Info.md","category":"E","quote":null,"cells":["Current transfer value","£3,002.02"]},{"passageId":"P24","source":"Standard_Life_Policy Value.md","category":"E","quote":"£2,994.30","cells":null},{"passageId":"P16","source":"Standard_Life_Policy_Info.md","category":"E","quote":"SL At Retirement Universal (PP10 Year)Pension\n100.00%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P5