re repeated verbatim across Aviva, Zurich and Standard Life recommendations ('wider range of investment options', 'adviser charges to be deducted directly', 'actively monitor and adjust investments'). Under the guard, identical bullets repeated verbatim are boilerplate; they should not all be marked isClientSpecific=true. Third, the ATR override from 4 to 5 is not documented in the risk profile file — the 'Agreed risk level' section records no additional notes — leaving the basis for the agreed rating unsupported. Fourth, no retirement income projection exists, weakening the suitability narrative for OBJ3. Fifth, C2's financial position and risk profile are absent, so the report cannot be verified as suitable for the joint client. The vulnerability overlay: no specific vulnerability indicators are identified in the available evidence that would materially alter this assessment. On balance, the Standard Life cost contradiction (a rationale claiming a saving where the evidence shows an increase, compounded by the wrong base value being used) is a material concern sufficient to warrant a Potential Concern finding at High severity, reinforced by the boilerplate issue and the undocumented ATR override.","citations":[{"passageId":"P8","source":"Test Case 1 - Policy Research -2025.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Recommendation","Switch","Which objective/ goal is this achieving?","","Why/Why isnt this scheme suitable for the client?","Lifestyle, expensive, no adviser servicing"]},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Test Case 1 - Policy Research -2025.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Recommendation","Switch","Which objective/ goal is this achieving?","","Why/Why isnt this scheme suitable for the client?","Expensive, no adviser servicing"]},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Test Case 1 - Policy Research -2025.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Recommendation","Retain","Which objective/ goal is this achieving?","","Why/Why isnt this scheme suitable for the client?"