mance). The report does present non-cost benefits for each switch (investment choice, fund availability at risk level 5, retirement flexibility, adviser charging facilitation, lifestyling concerns) and the file notes (P18) corroborate the research basis for discounting alternatives. The guard — a cheaper option rejected for evidenced non-cost reasons — applies to Zurich and Aviva where the rationale is predominantly non-cost. However, for Standard Life, the report positively claims a cost saving that is contradicted by its own table and is computed on the wrong fund value. This is a material internal contradiction that cannot be explained away by the guard, because the report is not rejecting a cheaper alternative on non-cost grounds — it is affirmatively claiming a cost saving that does not hold up. Transaction costs are excluded with a stated reason (variable, reflected in performance figures net of charges — P8), which is a Moderate concern per the decision logic. The vulnerability overlay: no vulnerability characteristics have been identified in the evidence that would materially alter this assessment. Outcome: Potential Concern at High severity, driven by the Standard Life cost claim contradiction and the wrong-base arithmetic in the charges table.","citations":[{"passageId":"P10","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"Lower Costs - The receiving scheme has a lower overall cost structure compared to your existing pension, meaning more of your savings remain invested for growth rather than being lost to charges. The plan itself is 0.08% more expensive than the recommended solution","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":null,"cells":["Standard Life","0.18%","£186.19","+0.26%","£268.94"]},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"the Aviva plan is 0.24% less expensive than your current plans","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitabilit