The maximum level of Benefits You can take through Capped Drawdown is calculated at the Initial Calculation Point. The maximum level of Benefits is recalculated after three years and at the end of each subsequent period of three years (called a Reference Period), up until You reach the age of 75. After this, the maximum allowed must be recalculated annually.
If the value of Your Capped Drawdown Benefits under Your Pension Portfolio is reduced because:
