Market orders are placed online outside of a Model Portfolio and are immediately sent to Our nominated stockbroker to be executed.
All orders and regular orders (payments or withdrawals) made within a Model Portfolio, will be instructed as scheduled market orders.
Scheduled market orders are placed online and submitted to Our nominated stockbroker three times a day at 10am, 1pm and 3pm. It may also be a policy of Our nominated stockbroker that orders will be aggregated. This means that the price of securities may rise or fall in the period between the receipt of Your order and the time it is actioned. Events which could result in a different price being secured include but are not limited to:
trades instructed outside normal market size resulting in a price which is different from that which would have prevailed on a single deal; and/or
a delay between orders being placed with Us and then being placed in the market whilst market movement takes place, resulting in price movements which could be either favourable or unfavourable; and/or
PTM levies being triggered for trades over £10,000.
