on.","The file contains no evidence that a vulnerability assessment was conducted at any stage of the advice process, meaning the 'NotAssessed' status in the report is neither corroborated nor contradicted by a completed assessment record.","C1 is aged 70 (DOB 07/06/1956, age recorded as 70 in fact find P3), which is an FG21/1 life-stage driver warranting explicit consideration of vulnerability, yet no screening or consideration is recorded in any document.","The file notes (P1) discuss ATR and capacity for loss at length but are entirely silent on vulnerability screening, FG21/1 considerations, or any duty-of-care overlay for a 70-year-old client.","No accessible format assessment beyond a 'No Requirement' tick-box (P10) is evidenced; no record of how comprehension or communication needs were explored is present in any document."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":[],"analysis":"The decision logic requires: (a) both absent — no issue; (b) file records a vulnerability the report never acknowledges — potential concern; (c) report asserts vulnerability with no file record — potential concern. Here, no vulnerability is positively recorded in either the report or the file. On a strict 'both absent' reading this would be no issue. However, the check runs as an overlay on all cases and FG21/1 imposes an affirmative obligation to consider and record vulnerability screening, not merely to record identified characteristics. C1 is 70 years old — an age that under FG21/1 constitutes a life-stage driver requiring explicit consideration. The fact find records no vulnerability screening section having been completed beyond a 'No Requirement' accessible format tick-box (P10). The file notes (P1) are detailed on ATR and capacity for loss but wholly silent on vulnerability. The risk profile report (P13) records no additional notes in either relevant section. There is no record anywhere of how, when, or by whom vulnerability was considered. The 'NotAssessed' status in the canonical model is therefore not a finding that vulnerability was considered and nothing found; it reflects that no assessment was conducted or recorded at all. For a 70-year-old client undergoing a consolidation of five pension plans — a significant financial transaction — the complete absence of any vulnerability screening record meets the 'High' severity threshold under the guidance: no vulnerability assessment anywhere in a case with a clear FG21/1 driver (age/life-stage). The guard that age alone is not a vulnerability characteristic is noted: this finding is not that age constitutes a vulnerability, but that the presence of a 70-year-old client is a recognised FG21/1 driver that requires the question to be asked and recorded, and there is no evidence it was.","citations":[{"passageId":"P3","source":"Fact Find (Test 1).md","category":"B","quote":null,"cells":["Date of Birth","07/06/1956"]},{"passageId":"P3","source":"Fact Find (Test 1).md","category":"B","quote":null,"cells":["Age","70"]},{"passageId":"P10","source":"Fact Find (Test 1).md","category":"B","quote":null,"cells":["Accessible format requirement","No Requirement"]},{"passageId":"P13","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":"No additional notes were recorded","cells":null},{"passageId":"P1","source":"File notes notes - updated.md","category":"C","quote":"XXXX, you are aware that investment values can rise as well as fall, and although your experience is limited to your workplace pension arrangements, you understand that returns are not guaranteed. You confirmed that any potential underperformance would not have a detrimental impact on your day-to-day living.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P7","source":"Fact Find (Test 1).md","category":"B","quote":"Preferred delivery method\n\nNo Preference","cells":null}],"severity":"High","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

